@crowmagnumb your API is broken: it should answer 204 if there is no content, adapt your client so that it can deal with by using `responseType: "text"`.

This is not a bug, `HttpClient` became stricter lately, I suppose to more easily detect this kind of implicit situations where you think something while something else is happening…

(but `HttpClient` is also broken because of https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/19413 because it shouldn't try to parse the body with a 204 status).
